    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d119">

                <pb facs="0180" n="115" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg115"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/3898: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-03-09T16:00:00+01:00">March 9, 1936—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 9—1:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>85. My telegram No. 78, March 6, 10 a.m.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d119-f1"/> The
                    Ethiopian Minister at Paris yesterday addressed a communication to the Secretary
                        General<anchor n="4" xml:id="d119-f2"/> reiterating the Emperor’s acceptance
                    of the [proposal of the?] Committee of Thirteen and placing himself at the
                    Committee’s disposal for any further information desired.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d119-f1" n="3" xml:id="d119-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d119-f2" n="4" xml:id="d119-f2-content">
                <p>For text of Ethiopian reply, dated March 5, 1936, see League of Nations, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Official Journal</hi>, April 1936, p. 395.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
